{{Term/Store|Wild Horses||Series, BotW}} is a [[Side Quest]] in {{BotW}}.<ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Wild Horses}}<br/>{{Color BotW|Side Quest|Dueling Peaks Stable}}|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref>

==Overview==
When [[Link]] asks [[Rensa]] at [[Dueling Peaks Stable]] about wild [[Horse]]s for a second time, he will remark that there is no feeling like taming one.<ref>{{Cite|They're wild, so 'til you calm 'em, it's gonna be one crazy ride. But there's no feeling quite like taming a wild stallion!|Rensa|BotW}}</ref> He asserts his authority on the matter, as he came in second place at the [[Hyrule Horse-Taming Competition]].<ref>{{Cite|Trust me—I took second place in the Hyrule Horse-Taming Competition!|Rensa|BotW}}</ref> Rensa notices the look that Link gives him,<ref>{{Cite|HEY!<br/>I saw that look you gave me!<br/>...|Rensa|BotW}}</ref> and therefore decides to challenge him to a "tame-off".<ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Fine!}} You don't believe me? Let's go, pal! You and me. Right here. Right now. You want to challenge the second-place Hyrule Horse Taming Competition winner to a tame-off?! YOU GOT IT, MISTER!|Rensa|BotW}}</ref>

If Link agrees, Rensa explains that he must bring a [[Wild Horse]] back to the [[Stable]] within the time limit.<ref>{{Cite|[Uhh... OK.] That's the spirit! The only rule is that you must bring a wild horse back to this spot within the time limit!|Rensa|BotW}}</ref> Link can bring back any Horse he finds, especially since the surrounding area is full of them.<ref>{{Cite|This area is chock full of wild horses. Any one of them will do!|Rensa|BotW}}</ref> To beat Rensa's record, Link will need to retrieve the Horse within two minutes.<ref>{{Cite|My record is two minutes flat, so you need to bring back a wild horse within that time.|Rensa|BotW}}</ref> He tells Link to prepare for taming,<ref>{{Cite|PREPARE FOR EXTREME TAMING!|Rensa|BotW}}</ref> at which point both the [[Side Quest]] and the timer begins.{{Note|If a Wild Horse is nearby when Link attempts to start the Hyrule Horse-Taming Competition, he will not be able to participate. However, it is possible to summon [[Epona]] with the [[Amiibo (Ability)|amiibo]] [[Rune]] immediately upon starting, which counts as a win.}}

The goal of the Hyrule Horse-Taming Competition is to bring a Horse back to Rensa in under two minutes. Several groups of Wild Horses can be found near the Stable, though if Link travels too far away, Rensa will call out and disqualify him.<ref>{{Cite|Hey, where are you going?|Rensa|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|If you go too far, then I can't record an accurate time. Could you try to stay at least somewhat near the stable?|Rensa|BotW}}</ref> While participating in the Hyrule Horse-Taming Competition, Link cannot [[Warping|Warp]] to any [[Travel Gate]]s or the [[Travel Medallion]].<ref>{{Cite|You can't travel from here.|Sheikah Slate|BotW}}</ref>

Once Link manages to bring a Horse within the time limit, Rensa is shocked that his record was beaten so easily.<ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Amazing!}} But...I can't believe you beat my two-minute record so easily...|Rensa|BotW}}</ref>{{Note|If Link fails to make the time limit, Rensa will note that breaking two minutes is no easy task, and he encourages Link by telling him it took years of practice to win second place in the Hyrule Horse-Taming Competition.<ref>{{Cite|Hahaha! Breaking the two-minute mark is pretty tough, right? But don't be discouraged. I mean, it took me years of practice to place second in the Hyrule Horse-Taming Competition.|Rensa|BotW}}</ref>}} He admits that, while he won second place in the Hyrule Horse-Taming Competition, the only participants were himself and his brother.<ref>{{Cite|I mean, I won second place in the Hyrule Horse-Taming Competition! To be fair, it was just my brother and I competing...|Rensa|BotW}}</ref> As a reward, Rensa gives Link a [[Purple Rupee]].<ref>{{Cite|Anyway, here's the purse for winning the second official Hyrule Horse-Taming Competition! You earned it.|Rensa|BotW}}</ref> Rensa realizes that, since there is more Horse-taming competition out there than he thought, [[Hyrule]] must not be as bad as he thought.<ref>{{Cite|I guess there's more competition out there than I knew about. Maybe Hyrule isn't all bad after all!|Rensa|BotW}}</ref> When he finishes speaking, the Side Quest will be completed.

